{ "Identifier":           {"ImplementerID": "1", "ImplementationID": "MMC-EDP-V2.5-I01", "AIMName": "1MMC-EDP-V2.5-I01"},
  "Header":               "MMC-EDP-V2.5",

  "APIProfile":           "Basic",
  "Description":          "Entity Dialogue Processing: produces the Machine's Text and Personal Status from the human's Text, its Text Descriptors, the human's Personal Status and identity, the identifiers of the scene's objects, and the Basic Audio-Visual Scene, using the running Summary as dialogue memory. In Audio Scene Management (CAE-ASM), given the Audio Scene the User edits, it turns what the User says into User Commands for CAE-ASM, says what was done or asks when the request is unclear, and tells the User Agent, as Text For UA, what only the User Agent does: undo, save, stop.",

